NOTICE

This work derives from the "ipguard" package for pfSense software by Marcello
Coutinho, distributed as part of Unofficial-pfSense-packages:

    https://github.com/marcelloc/Unofficial-pfSense-packages

Changes made to the original:

  * ipguard.inc: $new_config is initialised before it is used. It was declared
    only inside a branch that a fresh install never enters, so count() received
    null and aborted the installation outright under PHP 8.

  * ipguard.inc: the service now starts when there is anything to guard. The
    condition also tested $ipguard['enable'], a variable left over from the
    preceding foreach -- so whether the service ran depended on the last entry
    in the list rather than on any of them.

  * ipguard.inc: the deinstall command passed the result of glob() to
    unlink_if_exists(), which globs its argument itself -- so pfSense's own
    glob() received an array and threw under PHP 8, leaving the package's
    config files behind when it was removed.

  * ipguard.inc: removed a duplicated file_put_contents that wrote the same
    file twice, and the pfSense 2.2 PBI symlink workaround. PBI was retired
    with pfSense 2.3 in 2016 and /usr/pbi does not exist on any supported
    release.

  * Packaging: built and installed as a real pfSense-pkg-IPguard, so it appears
    in and can be removed from System > Package Manager. See docs/PACKAGING.md.
